{"repositoryId":743512308,"availability":"available","full":"FindAllTeam/FindAll","name":"FindAll","description":"Automated analysis of network security emergency response tools.（自动化分析网络安全应急响应工具）","category":"Developer tools","language":null,"stars":752,"forks":50,"created":"2024-01-15T11:54:33Z","updated":"2024-06-17T02:09:54Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://findallteam.github.io","topics":[],"demo":"https://findallteam.github.io/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:41.609Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:41.609Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:41.609Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T13:37:41.609Z","stars":752,"forks":50}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["FindAll is a dedicated emergency response tool designed for network security blue teams to help team members respond to and analyze network security threats effectively. It integrates advanced information gathering and automated analysis capabilities to improve the efficiency and accuracy of security incident response.","FindAll adopts a client-server (CS) architecture that is particularly suitable for scenarios where users cannot directly log in to remote hosts for security checks. In such cases, operators with appropriate permissions only need to run FindAll's Agent component on the target hosts to collect necessary data.","The data is then downloaded locally for in-depth analysis by security experts through FindAll's intuitive graphical user interface (GUI). FindAll's interface is clean and straightforward, allowing users without extensive knowledge of complex command lines to get started easily, greatly lowering the barrier to entry."],"features":["System basics: Outputs detailed system info and checks config and patches to identify vulnerabilities.","Network info: Analyzes current network connections. With Threatbook API, easily identifies abnormal networks, locates corresponding processes for analysis.","Startup items: Examines auto-start programs.","Scheduled tasks: Detects potentially malicious scheduled tasks.","Process investigation: Identifies and analyzes suspicious processes to quickly locate backdoors."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FindAllTeam/FindAll/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1a50e4c04b4934e28f17c58076753dc3fe82980c36a75b5e34d20be8f6fce03a","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:41.766Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:41.766Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"FindAll is a dedicated emergency response tool designed for network security blue teams to help team members respond to and analyze network security threats effectively. It integrates advanced information gathering and automated analysis capabilities to improve the efficiency and accuracy of security incident response.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FindAllTeam/FindAll/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"FindAll is a dedicated emergency response tool designed for network security blue teams to help team members respond to and analyze network security threats effectively. It integrates advanced information gathering and automated analysis capabilities to improve the efficiency and accuracy of security incident response.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FindAllTeam/FindAll/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"FindAll adopts a client-server (CS) architecture that is particularly suitable for scenarios where users cannot directly log in to remote hosts for security checks.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FindAllTeam/FindAll/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Adopts client-server architecture for one-click local scans or remote scanning via Agent, suitable when direct remote login is not possible.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FindAllTeam/FindAll/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"1a50e4c04b4934e28f17c58076753dc3fe82980c36a75b5e34d20be8f6fce03a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FindAllTeam/FindAll/b